#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:151
msgid ""
"The database has been used with a more recent version of digiKam and has "
"been updated to a database schema which cannot be used with this version. "
"(This means this digiKam version is too old, or the database format is to "
"recent) Please use the more recent version of digikam that you used before. "
msgstr ""
"De Datenbank wöör mit en nieger Verschoon vun digiKam bruukt, disse hett de "
"Datenbank op en Schema opfrischt, mit dat disse Verschoon nix anfangen kann. "
"(Dat bedüüdt: Disse Verschoon is to oolt, oder dat Datenbankformaat is to "
"nieg. Bruuk bitte de nieger digiKam-Verschoon, de Du al bruukt hest. "

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:215
msgid ""
"Failed to create tables in database.\n"
" "
msgstr ""
"Fehler bi't Opstellen vun Tabellen binnen de Datenbank.\n"
" "

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:244
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"The schema updating process from version 4 to 5 failed, caused by an error "
"that we did not expect. You can try to discard your old database and start "
"with an empty one. (In this case, please move the database files \"%1\" and "
"\"%2\" from the directory \"%3\"). More probably you will want to report "
"this error to the digikam-devel@kde.org mailing list. As well, please have a "
"look at what digiKam prints on the console. "
msgstr ""
"Dat Opfrischen vun dat Datenbankschema vun 4 to 5 is fehlslaan, dat geev en "
"Fehler, den keeneen verwacht hett. Du kannst nu de ole Datenbank wegsmieten "
"un mit en leddige nieg anfangen (maak de Dateien \"%1\" un \"%2\" ut den "
"Orner \"%3\" weg, wenn Du dat wullt). Beter is dat wull, wenn Du dissen "
"Fehler op de Nettpostlist digikam-devel@kde.org künnig maakst. Kiek bitte "
"ok, wat digiKam na de Konsool utgifft. "

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:701
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"Failed to copy the old database file (\"%1\")to its new location (\"%2\")."
"Please make sure that the file can be copied, or delete it."
msgstr ""
"Dat Koperen vun de ole Datenbankdatei (\"%1\") na ehr niege Steed (\"%2\") "
"is fehlslaan. Beseker bitte, wat sik de Datei koperen lett, oder do ehr weg."

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:714
msgid "Copied database file"
msgstr "Datenbankdatei kopeert"

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:718
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"The old database file (\"%1\") has been copied to the new location (\"%2\") "
"but it cannot be opened. Please delete both files and try again, starting "
"with an empty database. "
msgstr ""
"De ole Datenbankdatei (\"%1\") wöör na de niege Steed (\"%2\") kopeert, man "
"lett sik nich opmaken. Do disse twee Dateien bitte all beed weg un fang "
"nochmaal mit en leddig Datenbank an. "

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:733
msgid "Opened new database file"
msgstr "Nieg Datenbankdatei opmaakt"

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:751
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"Could not update from the old SQLite2 file (\"%1\"). Please delete this file "
"and try again, starting with an empty database. "
msgstr ""
"De ole SQLite2-Datei (\"%1\") lett sik nich opfrischen. Do disse Datei bitte "
"weg un fang nochmaal mit en leddig Datenbank an. "

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:763
msgid "Updated from 0.7 database"
msgstr "Vun 0.7-Datenbank opfrischt"

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:823
msgid "Prepared table creation"
msgstr "Opstellen vun en Tabell praatmaakt"

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:832
msgid "Created tables"
msgstr "Tabellen opstellt"

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:844
msgid ""
"No album library path has been found in the configuration file. Giving up "
"the schema updating process. Please try with an empty database, or repair "
"your configuration."
msgstr ""
"Binnen Dien Instellendatei lett sik keen Padd na en Albensammeln finnen. Dat "
"Opfrischen vun't Schema warrt nu opgeven. Versöök dat mit en leddig "
"Datenbank nochmaal, oder richt Dien Instellendatei."

#: libs/database/schemaupdater.cpp:862
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"There was an error associating your albumLibraryPath (\"%1\") with a storage "
"volume of your system. This problem may indicate that there is a problem "
"with your installation. If you are working on Linux, check that HAL is "
"installed and running. In any case, you can seek advice from the digikam-"
"devel@kde.org mailing list. The database updating process will now be "
"aborted because we do not want to create a new database based on false "
"assumptions from a broken installation."
msgstr ""
"Dat geev en Fehler bi't Towiesen vun Dien Albumsammeln-Padd (\"%1\")na en "
"Spiekerreedschap vun Dien Systeem. Dat mag angahn, dat gifft en Problem mit "
"Dien Installatschoon. Löppt dor en Linux bi Di, kiek bitte, wat HAL "
"installeert is un löppt. Du kannst ok op de Nettpostlist digikam-devel@kde."
"org na Raat fragen. Dat Opfrischen vun de Datenbank warrt nu afbraken, nüms "
"bruukt en Datenbank, de op lege Daten ut en schaadhaftig Installeren opbuut "
"wöör."

