#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:76
msgid "Photographer Information"
msgstr "Informatschonen över den Fotograaf"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:79
msgid "Author:"
msgstr "Maker:"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:84
msgid ""
"<p>This field should contain your name, or the name of the person who "
"created the photograph. If it is not appropriate to add the name of the "
"photographer (for example, if the identify of the photographer needs to be "
"protected) the name of a company or organization can also be used. Once "
"saved, this field should not be changed by anyone. This field does not "
"support the use of commas or semi-colons as separator. \n"
"This field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Hier schall Dien Naam oder de vun den Fotograaf stahn. Is dat nich "
"mööglich oder nich wullt (wenn a.B. den Fotograaf sien Naam schuult warrn "
"mutt), kannst Du hier ok den Naam vun en Sellschap oder Organisatschoon "
"bruken. Na't Sekern mutt nüms dat mehr ännern. Dat Feld ünnerstütt keen "
"Kommas oder Streekpünkt as Trennteken un kann tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens "
"bargen</p>"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:90
msgid "Author Title:"
msgstr "Maker sien Titel:"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:95
msgid ""
"<p>This field should contain the job title of the photographer. Examples "
"might include titles such as: Staff Photographer, Freelance Photographer, or "
"Independent Commercial Photographer. Since this is a qualifier for the "
"Author field, the Author field must also be filled out. \n"
"This field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Hier schall den Fotograaf sien Profeschoon-Beteken stahn. Bispillen sünd "
"\"Produktenfotograaf\", \"Freeschapen Fotograaf\" oder \"Fotokünstler\". Dit "
"is en Angaav bito dat Maker-Feld, dor muttst Du ok wat infögen.\n"
"Dat Feld kann tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:109
msgid "Credit and Copyright"
msgstr "Dank un Copyright"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:112
msgid "Credit:"
msgstr "Dank:"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:117
msgid ""
"<p>(synonymous to Provider): Use the Provider field to identify who is "
"providing the photograph. This does not necessarily have to be the author. "
"If a photographer is working for a news agency such as Reuters or the "
"Associated Press, these organizations could be listed here as they are "
"\"providing\" the image for use by others. If the image is a stock "
"photograph, then the group (agency) involved in supplying the image should "
"be listed here. \n"
"This field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>(liek as Anbeder): Mit dat Anbeder-Feld kannst Du angeven, wokeen dat "
"Bild praatstellt. Dat mutt nich jümmers de Maker wesen, wenn he för en "
"Narichtenagentur arbeidt, as Reuters oder Associated Press. Disse Bedrieven "
"köönt denn hier stahn, se stellt dat Bild för den Bruuk praat. Kummt dat "
"Bild ut den Vörraat vun en Agentur, schall se hier stahn.\n"
"Dit Feld kann tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:124
msgid "Source:"
msgstr "Born:"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:129
msgid ""
"<p>The Source field should be used to identify the original owner or "
"copyright holder of the photograph. The value of this field should never be "
"changed after the information is entered following the image's creation. "
"While not yet enforced by the custom panels, you should consider this to be "
"a \"write-once\" field. The source could be an individual, an agency, or a "
"member of an agency. To aid in later searches, it is suggested to separate "
"any slashes \"/\" with a blank space. Use the form \"photographer / agency\" "
"rather than \"photographer/agency.\" Source may also be different from "
"Creator and from the names listed in the Copyright Notice.\n"
"This field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Dat Feld \"Born\" warrt för den Orginaaleegner oder den Eegner vun't "
"Copyright bruukt. Na't Opstellen vun't Bild schull nüms dat mehr Feld "
"ännern. Dat warrt noch nich verdwungen, man liekers, bruuk dat Feld bitte as "
"bloots eenmaal schriefbor. As Born schall en Persoon, en Agentur oder en "
"Agenturliddmaat angeven warrn. As Ünnerstütten för later Söökanfragen giff "
"bitte vör un achter Dwarsstreek Freetekens in, also nich \"Fotograaf/Agentur"
"\", man beter \"Fotograaf / Agentur\". De Born kann wat anners wesen as de "
"Maker oder de Naams bi Copyright.\n"
"Dit Feld kann tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:138
msgid "Copyright:"
msgstr "Copyright:"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:143
msgid ""
"<p>The Copyright Notice should contain any necessary copyright notice for "
"claiming the intellectual property, and should identify the current owner(s) "
"of the copyright for the photograph. Usually, this would be the "
"photographer, but if the image was done by an employee or as work-for-hire, "
"then the agency or company should be listed. Use the form appropriate to "
"your country. USA: &copy; {date of first publication} name of copyright "
"owner, as in \"&copy;2005 John Doe.\" Note, the word \"copyright\" or the "
"abbreviation \"copr\" may be used in place of the &copy; symbol. In some "
"foreign countries only the copyright symbol is recognized and the "
"abbreviation does not work. Furthermore the copyright symbol must be a full "
"circle with a \"c\" inside; using something like (c) where the parentheses "
"form a partial circle is not sufficient. For additional protection "
"worldwide, use of the phrase, \"all rights reserved\" following the notice "
"above is encouraged. \n"
"In Europe you would use: Copyright {Year} {Copyright owner}, all rights "
"reserved. \n"
"In Japan, for maximum protection, the following three items should appear in "
"the copyright field of the IPTC Core: (a) the word, Copyright; (b) year of "
"the first publication; and (c) name of the author. You may also wish to "
"include the phrase \"all rights reserved.\"\n"
"This field is limited to 128 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>De Kopeerrecht-Angaav schall all nödige Informatschonen bargen, de dat "
"Recht an't intellektuelle Egendom kloorstellt un angeven, wokeen dat "
"opstunns hett. Normalerwies is dat de Fotograaf, man wenn dat en "
"Opdragarbeidt weer oder he för en Bedrief arbeidt, schall de hier stahn. "
"Bruuk de Form, de för Dien Land gellt. USA: &copy; {Johr vun't eerste "
"Apenmaken} Naam vun den Rechtenholler, a.B.: \"&copy; 2005 Klaas Achterndiek"
"\". Ansteed dat \"&copy;\"-Symbool laat sik ok dat Woort \"Copyright\" oder "
"de Afkörten \"copr\" bruken. In en Reeg Länner gellt aver bloots dat Symbool "
"wat. Ok de Formen \"(c)\" un \"(C)\" langt nich. Goot is ok, wenn Du achter "
"de baven angeven Bemarken de Wöör \"all rights reserved\" bruukst.\n"
"In Europa is en propper Form: \"Copyright {Johr} {Rechtenholler}, all rights "
"reserved\".\n"
"In Japan schöölt disse Indrääg binnen dat Copyright-Feld stahn: a) dat Woort "
"\"Copyright\", b) dat Johr vun't eerste Apenmaken, un c) de Naam vun den "
"Maker. Ok hier kannst Du \"all rights reserved\" tofögen.\"\n"
"Dit Feld kann tohööchst 128 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:169
msgid ""
"<b>Note: These information are used to set <b><a href='http://en.wikipedia."
"org/wiki/Extensible_Metadata_Platform'>XMP</a></b> and <b><a href='http://en."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/IPTC'>IPTC</a></b> tags contents. There is no limitation "
"with XMP, but take a care that IPTC text tags only support the printable "
"<b><a href='http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ascii'>ASCII</a></b> characters set "
"and limit strings size. Use contextual help for details.</b>"
msgstr ""
"<p><b>Beacht bitte</b>: Disse Informatschonen warrt na <b><a href='http://de."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/Extensible_Metadata_Platform'>XMP</a></b>- un <b><a "
"href='http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPTC-NAA-Standard'>IPTC</a></b>-Feller "
"sekert. För XMP gifft dat keen Grenz, man för IPTC laat sik bloots de "
"druckboren <b><a href='http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ascii'>ASCII</a></b>-"
"Tekens un en fastleggt Bookstaventall bruken. Bruuk dat Rechtsklickmenü, "
"wenn Du mehr weten wullt.</p>"

#: utilities/setup/setupcollections.cpp:90
msgid "Root Album Folders"
msgstr "Wörtelalbum-Ornern"

#: utilities/setup/setupcollections.cpp:92
msgid ""
"Below are the locations of your root albums used to store your images. Write "
"access is necessary to be able to edit images in these albums.\n"
"Note: removable media (such as USB drive or DVD) and remote file systems "
"(such as NFS or Samba) are supported."
msgstr ""
"Nerrn staht de Padden na de Wörtelalben mit Dien Biller. Schriefverlööf deit "
"noot, wenn Du Dien Biller dor binnen ok bewerken wullt.\n"
"Du kannst ok tuuschbor Medien as USB oder DVDs un deelt Dateisystemen as NFS "
"oder Samba bruken."

#: utilities/setup/setupcollections.cpp:113
msgid "Database File Path"
msgstr "Datenbank-Dateipadd"

#: utilities/setup/setupcollections.cpp:115
msgid ""
"The location where the database file will be stored on your system. There is "
"one common database file for all root albums.\n"
"Write access is required to be able to edit image properties.\n"
"Note: a remote file system, such as NFS, cannot be used here."
msgstr ""
"Dit is de Steed, woneem de Datenbankdatei wohrt warrt. Dat is för all "
"Wörtelalben bloots een Datei.\n"
"Schriefverlööf deit noot, wenn Du de Bildegenschappen bewerken wullt.\n"
"Beacht bitte: Feern Dateisystemen, as NFS, laat sik hier nich bruken."

#: utilities/setup/setupcollections.cpp:193
msgid ""
"You don't seem to have write access to this database folder.\n"
"Without this access, the caption and tag features will not work."
msgstr ""
"As't lett hest Du keen Schriefverlöven för dissen Datenbank-Orner.\n"
"De Titel- un Slötelwoortfunkschonen laat sik so nich bruken."

#: utilities/setup/setupeditor.cpp:90
msgid "&Use theme background color"
msgstr "&Muster-Achtergrundklöör bruken"

#: utilities/setup/setupeditor.cpp:93
msgid "Enable this option to use background theme color in image editor area"
msgstr ""
"Maak dit an, wenn Du de Achtergrundklöör vun dat Muster binnen den "
"Bildeditor bruken wullt."

#: utilities/setup/setupeditor.cpp:102
msgid "Customize the background color to use in image editor area."
msgstr "Hier kannst Du de Achtergrundklöör för den Bildeditor utsöken."

#: utilities/setup/setupeditor.cpp:105
#, kde-format
msgid "Use &horizontal thumbbar (needs to restart %1)"
msgstr "&Kimmrecht Vöransichtbalken bruken (%1 mutt nieg start warrn)"

#: utilities/setup/setupeditor.cpp:108
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, the thumbnails bar will be displayed horizontally "
"behind the image area. You need to restart editor for this option take "
"effect."
msgstr ""
"Is dit anmaakt, warrt de Vöransichtbalken kimmrecht achter dat Bildrebeet "
"wiest. Du muttst den Editor nieg starten, ehr de Ännern bruukt warrt."

#: utilities/setup/setupeditor.cpp:116
msgid "Use Raw Import Tool to handle Raw image"
msgstr "Rohimport-Warktüüch för Rohbild-Verarbeiden bruken"

#: utilities/setup/setupeditor.cpp:117
msgid ""
"Set this option to use Raw Import tool to load a RAW image. With this tool "
"you are able to customize indeep decoding settings."
msgstr ""
"Bruuk dit, wenn Du för't Laden vun Rohbiller dat Rohimport-Warktüüch bruken "
"wullt. Mit dat Warktüüch laat sik mehr Dekodeer-Instellen fastleggen."

#: utilities/setup/setupeditor.cpp:139
msgid "Customize color used in image editor to identify under-exposed pixels."
msgstr "De Klöör fastleggen, mit de de Bildeditor ünnerbelicht Pixels wiest"

#: utilities/setup/setupeditor.cpp:146
msgid "Customize color used in image editor to identify over-exposed pixels."
msgstr "De Klöör fastleggen, mit de de Bildeditor överbelicht Pixels wiest"

#: utilities/setup/setupcamera.cpp:92
msgid ""
"Here you can see the digital camera list used by digiKam via the Gphoto "
"interface."
msgstr ""
"Dit is de List mit Digitaalkameras, de \"digiKam\" över de Gphoto-"
